## How to Install EcoTrace in Your Browser

Since EcoTrace is an open-source browser extension and not yet on the Chrome Web Store, you can easily install it manually via the ZIP file or from the source code.

### 🛠️ Method 1: Installing via the ZIP Release (Easiest)
1. Download the latest `EcoTrace.zip` from the [Releases](https://github.com/Maxation/EcoTrace/releases) page.
2. Unzip (extract) the downloaded file into a folder on your computer.
3. Open your browser (Chrome, Brave, or Edge) and navigate to the Extensions page:
   * In Chrome/Brave: Open a new tab and type `chrome://extensions/`
4. In the top-right corner of the Extensions page, toggle the **"Developer mode"** (Entwicklermodus) switch to **ON**.
5. In the top-left corner, click the **"Load unpacked"** (Entpackte Erweiterung laden) button.
6. Select the folder where you unzipped the EcoTrace files.
7. 🎉 **Done!** The EcoTrace icon will appear in your extension bar, and it will now work automatically on Amazon product pages.

### 💻 Method 2: Installing from Source Code (For Developers)
1. Clone this repository to your local machine:
```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/Maxation/EcoTrace.git](https://github.com/Maxation/EcoTrace.git)
